G1125.def:
**γράφω**, [in LXX chiefly for כּתב ];
1. **to scrape, graze** (Hom.), and later (Hdt.) **to sketch, draw**.
2. **to write**;
(a) **of forming or tracing letters on writing material**: Jhn.8:[6], [[Gal.6.11|Gal.6:11]], [[2Th.3.17|2Th.3:17]];
(b) **to express in writing, commit to writing, record**: [[Luk.1.63|Luk.1:63]], [[Jhn.19.21, 22|Jhn.19:21, 22]] [[Rev.1.11, 19|Rev.1:11, 19]] al.; of scripture as a standing authority (Deiss., _BS_, 112ff.), γέγραπται, **it stands written** (Luther), [[Mat.4.4|Mat.4:4]], [[Mrk.7.6|Mrk.7:6]], [[Luk.4.8|Luk.4:8]], [[Rom.1.17|Rom.1:17]], [[1Co.1.31|1Co.1:31]], al.; id. before ἐν, [[Mrk.1.2|Mrk.1:2]], [[Act.1.20|Act.1:20]], al.; with accusative, **to write of**: [[Jhn.1.46|Jhn.1:46]], [[Rom.10.5|Rom.10:5]]; before περί, [[Mat.26.24|Mat.26:24]], [[Mrk.14.21|Mrk.14:21]], [[Jhn.5.46|Jhn.5:46]] al.; with dative (WM, §31, 4), [[Luk.18.31|Luk.18:31]] id. before ἵνα (M, _Pr._, 207f.), [[Mrk.12.19|Mrk.12:19]], [[Luk.20.28|Luk.20:28]]; κατὰ τ. γεγραμμένον, [[2Co.4.13|2Co.4:13]] γεγραμμένον ἐστί, [[Jhn.2.17|Jhn.2:17]] ἐγράφη, [[Rom.4.24|Rom.4:24]] ἐπ᾽ αὐτῷ γεγραμμένα, [[Jhn.12.16|Jhn.12:16]]
(with) of writing directions or information, with dative of person(s): [[Rom.15.15|Rom.15:15]], [[2Co.7.12|2Co.7:12]], al.;
(d) **of that which contains the record or message**: βιβλίον, [[Mrk.10.4|Mrk.10:4]], [[Jhn.21.25|Jhn.21:25]], [[Rev.5.1|Rev.5:1]]; τίτλον, [[Jhn.19.19|Jhn.19:19]] ἐπιστολήν, [[Act.23.25|Act.23:25]] ἐντολήν, [[Mrk.10.5|Mrk.10:5]] (cf. ἀπο-, ἐγ-, ἐπι-, κατα-, προ-).
(AS)

G1140.def:
**δαιμόνιον**, -ου, τό
(neut. of δαιμόνιος, -α, -ον, _divine_), [in LXX (so also in π; see MM, _Exp._, x) for שֵׁד, אֱלִיל, (frequently in To) ;]
1. as in cl.;
(a) **the Divine power, Deity** (Hdt., Plat., al.);
(b) **an inferior divinity, deity** or **demon** (as in magical π, Deiss., _BS_, 281; MM, _Exp._, x): ξένα δ., [[Act.17.18|Act.17:18]]
2. (a) in OT, heathen deities, false gods (e.g. [[Deu.32.17|Deu.32:17]], Psa.95 (96):5);
(b) in NT, **evil spirits, demons**: θύουσιν δαιμονίοις, [[1Co.10.20|1Co.10:20]] διδασκαλίαι δαιμονίων, [[1Ti.4.1|1Ti.4:1]] προσκυνεῖν τὰ δ., [[Rev.9.20|Rev.9:20]] ἄρχων τῶν δ., [[Mat.9.34|Mat.9:34]] especially (syn. with πνεῦμα ἀκάθαρτον) as operating upon and "possessing" (of. δαιμονίζομαι) men: [[Mat.11.18|Mat.11:18]], and al.; εἰσέρχεσθαι δ. εἰς. . ., [[Luk.8.30|Luk.8:30]] δ. ἔχειν, [[Luk.4.33|Luk.4:33]] δ. ἐκβάλλειν, [[Mat.7.22|Mat.7:22]] In the phrase πνεῦμα δαιμονίου ἀκαθάρτου, [[Luk.4.33|Luk.4:33]], the wider cl. usage (1. _b_) is recognised, ἀκ. being elsewhere in NT, the epithet of πν., and δ. = πν. ἀκ. (see _ICC_, in l; Cremer, 168)
(AS)

G1189.def:
**δέομαι**
(mid. of δέω, II, which see, as depon.) [in LXX for חנן, etc. ;]
**to want for oneself**;
1. **to want, need**:
(a) absol.;
(b) with genitive
2. **to beg, request, beseech, pray**;
(i) **in general**: absol., [[Act.26.3|Act.26:3]], WH; with genitive of person(s), [[Luk.5.12; 8.28; 38|Luk.5:12; 8:28; 38]] (ἐδεῖτο; T, ἐδέετο, cf. Veitch, see word δέω) 9:38, [[Act.8.34; 21.39|Act.8:34; 21:39]], [[2Co.5.20|2Co.5:20]], [[Gal.4.12|Gal.4:12]]; before ἵνα, [[Luk.9.40|Luk.9:40]] before τό, with inf., [[2Co.10.2|2Co.10:2]] with genitive of person(s) and of thing(s), [[2Co.8.4|2Co.8:4]]
(ii) **of prayer to God**: absol., [[Act.4.31|Act.4:31]] before εἴ πως, [[Rom.1.10|Rom.1:10]] ἵνα, [[Luk.21.36; 22.32|Luk.21:36; 22:32]]; εἰς τό, [[1Th.3.10|1Th.3:10]] ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ πρὸς τ. κύριον, ὅπως, [[Act.8.24|Act.8:24]] with genitive, τοῦ κυρίου, ὅπως, [[Mat.9.38|Mat.9:38]], [[Luk.10.2|Luk.10:2]]; τοῦ Θεοῦ, [[Act.10.2|Act.10:2]] before εἰ ἄρα, [[Act.8.22|Act.8:22]]†
_SYN._: αἰτέω, and cf. δέησις. (AS)

G1121.def:
**γράμμα**, -τος, τό
(γράφω), [in LXX for סֵפֶר, etc. ;]
1. **that which is traced** or **drawn, a picture**.
2. **that which is written**;
(1) **a character, letter**: [[Gal.6.11|Gal.6:11]]
(2) **a writing, a written document**;
(a) **a bill** or **account**: [[Luk.16.6|Luk.16:6]], 7;
(b) **a letter**: [[Act.28.21|Act.28:21]]
(with) τὰ ἱερὰ γ., **the sacred writings**, i.e. the OT: [[2Ti.3.15|2Ti.3:15]] (so in Philo, _Vit. Mos._, iii, 39) ;
(d) τὸ γ., **the letter**, the written word as an external authority in contrast with the direct influence of the Spirit as manifested in the new Covenant: [[Rom.2.27, 29; 7.6|Rom.2:27, 29 7:6]], [[2Co.3.6|2Co.3:6]], 7;
(3) τὰ γ., **letters**, i.e. **learning**: [[Jhn.7.15|Jhn.7:15]], [[Act.26.24|Act.26:24]]. (In π. an illiterate person is very frequently referred to as γράμματα μ᾽̀ εἰδότης, and this "never means anything else than inability to write": MM, _Exp._, x; but see also Cremer, 166; _DCG_, i, 202; ii, 584.)
† (AS)

G1106.def:
**γνώμη**, -ης, ἡ
(γιγνώσκω), [in LXX: [[Dan.2.15|Da TH 2:15]] (דָּת), [[Psa.83.3|Ps 82(83):3]] (סוֹד), elsewhere, chiefly II Es, for טְעֵם ;]
1. **a means of knowing, a token** (Theogn.).
2. In Attic writers, **the mind**, its operations and results (see Edwards, _Lex._, _App._, A);
(a) **mind, understanding**;
(b) **purpose, intention**: [[Act.20.3|Act.20:3]]
(with) **judgment, opinion**: [[1Co.1.10|1Co.1:10]], [[Rev.17.13|Rev.17:13]];
(d) **counsel, advice**: [[1Co.7.25, 40|1Co.7:25, 40]] [[2Co.8.10|2Co.8:10]], Phm 14;
(e) **royal purpose, decree** (as in Da, I and II Es): [[Rev.17.17|Rev.17:17]] (Cremer, 671).
† (AS)

G1175.def:
**δεισιδαιμονία**, -ας, ἡ
(δεισιδαίμων, which see);
1. **fear of the gods**;
(a) **piety, religion**;
(b) **superstition**.
2. Objectively, **a religion**: [[Act.25.19|Act.25:19]] (Cremer, 72, 682).†
(AS)
